------------------------------------------------------------------------
The false premise was accepted on all 6 runs. Asked directly, the
model declines; handed a premise, it builds on it, and the reasons it offers
are invented.

Regions it named that do not exist: North America. Meridian has five,
and the confident explanation around each one was invented to fit.

The mechanism is the same either way, and it is not moral failure. The model
produces the most plausible continuation, and a confident explanation IS the most
plausible continuation of a confident premise. Plausibility is all it optimises.
